cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MVS Analyzer in research, please cite it as below, together with the formula hash and engine version from your run_manifest.json."
title: "MVS Analyzer: measuring which metric detects a change on your own data"
abstract: >-
  MVS Analyzer is an offline Windows application that ranks candidate summary
  metrics (median, mean, SD, CV, MAD, IQR, normalized MAD/IQR, RMS, range) by
  measured false-alarm rate, power, robustness, split-half repeatability and
  bootstrap interval coverage, using resampling of the user's own measurements.
  It reports an explicit verdict per metric (difference, equivalence via TOST,
  insufficient data, not applicable), Cliff's delta with a bootstrap interval,
  the minimum detectable effect, and a tamper-evident run manifest.
type: software
